ghudson@cie.uoregon.edu (Greg Hudson) writes:

>Blatant spoilers re: cursing a bag of holding
>
>1. Bless an empty bag of holding.
>2. Pick up the bag, two potions of water and as many rocks as you 
>   can carry.
>3. Put rocks in bag.  Pick up more rocks.  Repeat #3 until you can't
>   carry a single rock more.
>4. Make the two potions of water into holy water and curse the bag 
>   of holding.
>5. Drop the bag.  (I believe items evaporate when you remove 
>   them then from a cursed bag of holding, but dropping it should 
>   be simplest.)
>   
>You should be able to carry, what, about twice as much in the 
>future.

This won't work.  The weight of the bag of holding before and after
step 4 will be constant--in fact that's what the bug is all about.
To exploit the bug, one has to remove items from the bag after step
4.  With enough items, the bag will then have negative weight.
Note however, that the negative weight is only beneficial for weight
transferred to the bag.  I vaguely remember checking the [pl9] code
some time ago and finding out that when nethack computes the weight
of one's inventory, it zeros out the negative weights in the
computation (but without zeroing out the weight variables themselves).
Therefore, carrying a -10 weight bag doesn't allow you to carry
more unless you put items in the bag (in which case it might as
well be blessed).

[Also, items put in bags increase the bag's weight by at least one,
therefore stuff bags of holding with heavy items (which includes
bunches of rocks of course).]

